\section{The abstention gate}{

An \code{abstain_gate} node reads the one verdict it consumes and abstains
when any of these holds: the upstream emitter abstained; the verdict is
\code{"no_effect"} and the metric \code{n} is below \code{params$n_min} (default 25); the
verdict is \code{"no_effect"} and the power proxy
\verb{|effect_mean| / (noise_sd / sqrt(n))} is below \code{params$z_floor} (default
2); or any metric named in \code{params$floors} (a named list of minima) is
below its floor. \code{params$mode} sets what an abstention does downstream:
\code{"flag"} (default) records it and continues, \code{"halt-branch"} skips the
descendants, \code{"reroute"} tells a downstream triangulation to drop the
gated lens and reconcile the survivors.
